{
  "id": "COMPOUND:23600 - PROTEIN:5811",
  "verbalization": "(+)-Menthol is implicated in the interaction with VMRC-LCP through a series of molecular pathways, with Caspase-5 acting as a central mediator. The evidence suggests that (+)-Menthol targets Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid, Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, and 5-Oxobrucine. All of these compounds ultimately have VMRC-LCP as their target. This indicates that (+)-Menthol may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving Caspase-5, which is a key enzyme in the regulation of apoptosis and cellular signaling. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting Caspase-5 suggests that the pathway may be a general one, potentially involving different metabolic or signaling pathways. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that (+)-Menthol influences VMRC-LCP via a cascade involving Caspase-5, highlighting the importance of this enzyme in the biological response to (+)-Menthol.",
